{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdJKiNNfUATx8iMaSHMy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your job has been running every night: `launchctl print` shows 6 runs, last exit code 1, and the error log has an entry for each night. A failing review step, a failing failure report and a failing notifier stacked up, so nothing ever got sent. I've fixed all three and written the causes up in `ANSWER.md`. I haven't tested any of it under launchd or with Telegram. I only checked the plist and the shell syntax, and ran `notify.sh` offline.\n\n**Causes:**\n1. **The review step fails:** under launchd, `claude -p` stops with \"Not logged in · Please run /login\". The job only had `PATH` set (no `USER`), the keychain can be locked at 02:30, and stdin was left open.\n2. **The script dies before reporting the failure:** in zsh, `status` is a read-only variable, so `status=$?` kills the script at line 19. That line sits between the `claude` call and the \"FAILED\" message, which is why you got no failure notes either.\n3. **`notify.sh` would also have failed without a trace:** `TG_BOT_TOKEN` isn't set under launchd, and the fallback keychain lookup fails while the keychain is locked, which exits the script before it sends anything. It never read the token in `config.toml`, and `curl` treated Telegram's error replies as success.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- **`nightly-review.zsh`:**\n  - uses `rc=$?` instead of `status=$?`\n  - feeds the prompt to `claude` on stdin\n  - logs each run's exit code and duration\n  - counts a run that exits 0 but writes nothing as a failure\n  - includes the end of Claude's error output in the failure message\n  - reads an optional login token from `~/.config/nightly-review/claude-token`\n- **`notify.sh`:** looks for the token in the environment, then the keychain, then `config.toml`. If there's no token or the send fails, it now writes an error to the log and exits with an error.\n- **plist:** adds `USER` and `HOME`, and connects stdin to `/dev/null`.\n\n**What you need to do on the Mac:**\n1. If the keychain is locked at night, run `claude setup-token` once and save the result to `~/.config/nightly-review/claude-token` (readable only by you).\n2. Reload the job, then run it once with `launchctl kickstart -k`.\n3. Break it on purpose once to check that the failure message arrives too.\n\n**Security issue:** `README.md` contains a Telegram bot token in plain text, and it's different from the one in `config.toml`. Rotate it and remove it from the README. Also check that the token in `config.toml` is the current one.\n\nThe two worklore stories I used described exactly this situation. I didn't report back to worklore that I'd used them, because your rules say not to report to external services."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1529,"cache_read_input_tokens":32009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1529},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5278bcf0-9aa1-4102-b0a3-bd9b4ae973ba","uuid":"8039afec-ee5d-4e3e-8667-588e5616d49b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:18:36.966Z","request_id":"req_011CgdJKi2nXj4TMjTFYnwAa"}
